  (text "VBUS DIVIDER DESIGN & VERIFICATION NOTES (docs/WIRING.md §6.2.1)\n- Owner decision (2026-11-26, #174): Use 0.5% E96 pair R1=130 kOhm, R2=162 kOhm.\n  (Alternative 1% E24 pair: R1=120k, R2=150k — NEVER mix E96 and E24 pairs!)\n- Ratio R2/(R1+R2) = 0.5548: VBUS=4.75V -> 2.635V (> VIH_max 2.53V);\n  VBUS=5.50V -> 3.051V (< VDD_min 3.18V). ESP_3V3 measured 3.34V [V2].\n- Max power ~0.11 mW; standard THT 1/4W metal-film +/-0.5% resistors suffice.\n- No ESD clamp diode added on J3 or VBUS sense (#174 / H4 decision).\n  R1 (130 kOhm) acts as series current limiter on VBUS sense.\n- Kconfig: CONFIG_USB_DEVICE_VBUS_SENSE_GPIO=18, BVALID_OVERRIDE=y, POLL=100ms.\n- Safety: PC VBUS MUST NOT touch J3 #1 (VCC_5V). Power ESP32-P4 via H2 BEFORE PC!" (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 21.59 135.89 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) (color 15 70 30 1.0)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "d85a490a-d754-54e9-9fc2-974a521ea98d")
  )
